{"availability":"available","full":"alezen9/revo-realms","name":"revo-realms","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":43,"forks":6,"created":"2025-01-04T21:36:41Z","updated":"2026-09-30T15:35:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://alezen9.github.io/revo-realms/","topics":[],"demo":"https://alezen9.github.io/revo-realms/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.451Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.451Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.451Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.451Z","stars":43,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I started this project to challenge myself — to see if I could actually build a game that’s fun, performant, and visually interesting. But more than that, I started it for my niece.","One day, while I was finishing the final lesson of the Three.js Journey course, she sat next to me and watched me play the game we had just built. She loved it. And something clicked: what if I made something for her — and for anyone else — to enjoy?","From there, Revo Realms was born. It began as a small idea and slowly turned into a sandbox for me to explore real-time rendering, physics, soft culling, procedural content, and all the beautiful chaos that comes with trying to balance realism and performance — something I’ve grown to deeply respect in AAA development."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alezen9/revo-realms/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"75c9d4077c1097959f7429958e4218184e673cc1c244ddd8b234844dea62bd16","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.558Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.558Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I started this project to challenge myself — to see if I could actually build a game that’s fun, performant, and visually interesting. But more than that, I started it for my niece.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alezen